# USAGE

# import all files in the import folder
# curator import

# import specific files/folders
# curator import file1 file2 folder1 folder2

# import only a specific format
# curator import --fmt=flac

# import only lyric files
# curator import --lyrics

# check library for data hygiene issues (missing cover images, missing lyrics, etc)
# curator check


# IMPORT ORDER OF OPERATIONS
# 1. Recursively search the import dir for music files X
# 2. Parse the music file's metadata X
# 2.1. Check that the file extension matches the format X
# 2.2. Attempt to fetch correct metadata if critical pieces are missing, fallback to moving it to a manual tagging folder
# 3. Identify formatted filename X
# 4. Identify formatted album folder name X
# 5. Check if library directory exists X
# 6. Check if library directory already contains the file, handle duplicate x
# 7. Check if library directory contains a cover image
# 7.1. Check import directory for a matching cover image
# 8. Check if library directory contains matching lyric file
# 8.1. Check import directory for a matching lyric file
# 9. Identify genre(s) using online service
# 10. Fetch missing metadata using online service
# 11. Create library album directory if it didn't exist X
# 11.1. Use ffmpeg to update and clean tags and write the file to the library directory
# 12. Fetch or move the relevant lyric file and place in library directory
# 13. Fetch or move relevant cover image and place in library directory
# 14. Validate changes
# 15. Remove imported file from import directory
# 16. Repeat

# CHECK ORDER OF OPERATIONS
# 1. Recursively search the library for:
#   - Missing cover images
#   - Missing lyric files
#   - Incomplete albums
#   - Incorrect tags / filename formats
# 2. Report issues and offer to resolve automatically
